    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Verdan Classes (Customizable Origins)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-custom-origin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-custom-origin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section assumes that you’re using the option “"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Customizing Your Origin",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/tcoe/character-options#CustomizingYourOrigin"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "” rules presented in Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything. If you’re not using those rules, scroll down to the next section."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With only a d8 hit die, Black Blood Healing is decently effective, and\n\tTelepathic Insight protects the Artificer’s two bad saves. You also get an\n\textra skill without piling on yet another tool."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For a class with relatively poor armor and and a big pool of hit points,\n\tBlack Blood Healing feels like nice insurance against poor hit die rolls. And\n\twhile rolling a 1 or a 2 certainly hurts, mathematically Black Bood Healing is\n\tnot going to save you."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An extra skill helps you expand beyond Face skills, and Black Blood Healing\n\tis reasonably effective with a d8 hit die. Telepathic Insight provides some\n\tprotection on one the Bard’s bad saves, and an extra skill will help you\n\texpand beyond Face skills."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Black Blood Healing is decent with a d8 hit die, but the Druid has no lack of\n\thealing options. Telepathic Insight is nice, but clerics are proficient in the\n\tsame saves so the benefits are less impactful. The extra skill never hurts,\n\tbut it’s hardly novel."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Black Blood Healing is decent with a d8 hit die, but the Druid has no lack of\n\thealing options. Telepathic Insight is nice, but druids are already excellent\n\tat Wisdom saves. The extra skill never hurts, but it’s hardly novel."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Black Blood Healing isn’t great with a d10 hit die, but an extra skill offers\n\tyou some sorely-needed options outside of combat, and Telepathic Insight\n\tprotects you from saves which are normally major vulernabilities for the\n\tFighter."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Monks tend to have poor AC at low levels, so you’re very reliant on hit dice\n\tto recover. Black Blood Healing can help there a little bit, especially with\n\tonly d8 hit dice. Telepathic Insight provides additional protection until\n\tDiamond Body comes online and you largely stop worrying about saving throws.\n\tAn extra skill helps close the skill gap with rogues."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Black Blood Healing feels silly on the Paladin due to both Lay on Hands and\n\ttheir large hit dice. An extra skill is great, but you can get that from\n\tnumerous other races. The Verdan’s telepathy is neat, but too limited to be\n\tparticularly exciting. Telepathic Insight covers the same saves as the\n\tPaladin’s proficiencies, and couple with Aura of Protection you really don’t\n\tneed the extra help there."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Black Blood Healing isn’t great with a d10 hit die, but an extra skill helps\n\tclose the skill gap with the Rogue and Telepathic Insight protects the Ranger\n\ton two of their bad saves."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An extra skill helps you cover more skill-based roles, Black Blood Healing is\n\treasonably effective with a d8 hit die, and Telepathic Insight protects you on\n\ttwo of the Rogue’s worst saves."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Black Blood Healing is at peak effectiveness with a d6 hit dice. An extra\n\tskill helps you expand beyond Face skills, and Telepathic Insight helps\n\tprotect one of your weak saves as well as making you basically infallibe at\n\tCharisma saves."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An extra skill helps you expand beyond Face skills, and Black Blood Healing\n\tis reasonably effective with a d8 hit die. Telepathic Insight reinforces the\n\tWarlock’s two good saves, so as long as you’re not worried about Insight or\n\tPerception, you can dump Wisdom with little consequence."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Black Blood Healing is at peak effectiveness with a d6 hit dice, and\n\tTelepathic Insight protects you on Charisma saves without needing to actually\n\tdegrade yourself by being charismatic. Wizards are proficient in Wisdom saves,\n\tbut often don’t have great Wisdom, so Telepathic Insight’s protection there is\n\tvery welcome."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
